#> tool: sedrepl
#> wait: sunless ocean
#> pause: 40
#> must: Down to a sunless ocean.
#> must: Where Alph, the sacred river, ran
#> not: sunless SEA
#> not: sunless sea.
#> source: s/SEA/ocean/
# 3. Commands run in order; each one sees the output of the last. McMahon 1.2
# The whole script is compiled before any input is read, then applied to each
# line one command at a time. The first s turns "sea" into "SEA"; the second
# s finds that "SEA" and makes it "ocean". Swap the two lines and the second
# substitution has nothing to match: the line comes out as "SEA".
# Try: swap the two s commands and save.
s/sea/SEA/
s/SEA/ocean/

#DATA
In Xanadu did Kubla Khan
A stately pleasure dome decree:
Where Alph, the sacred river, ran
Through caverns measureless to man
Down to a sunless sea.
